Enable the window button colour pickers when their checkbox changes

The page "Window button colors" of the style dialog holds nine background
pickers and eighteen icon pickers. Two checkboxes on the page "Window buttons"
own those columns. setWidgetOptions() called setEnabled(false) on the nine
background pickers when opts.titlebarButtons lacked TITLEBAR_BUTTON_COLOR. It
did the same for the eighteen icon pickers when the flag
TITLEBAR_BUTTON_ICON_COLOR was absent. No code called setEnabled(true) on those
pickers.

The user ticked "Use custom background colors", moved to the next page, and
found the pickers grey. The pickers came back only after a save of the options
and a new dialog.

The patch adds the function updateTitlebarButtonColorState(). The function sets
the state of the nine background pickers from the checkbox
titlebarButtons_custom. It sets the state of the eighteen icon pickers from the
checkbox titlebarButtons_customIcon. The function runs from the slot of each
checkbox, and from setWidgetOptions() in place of the two blocks of
setEnabled(false). The dialog still sets the colour of every picker at each
load, so a disabled picker keeps its colour.

The patch touches the Qt 6 configuration dialog alone. qt5/config and qt4/config
hold separate copies of the dialog, and each copy carries the same defect. This
package builds neither copy, because it sets QTC_QT5_ENABLE_KDE off and
ENABLE_QT4 off.

The change sits on the branch work/window-button-colors of the local tree. The
fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !10 on system/qtcurve holds
that branch as the source.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

